nm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T01:11:29-08:00","id":1503669,"title":"","content":"For a simple Storypath roll, set your dice pool, difficulty and enhancement.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Focus</b></u><ul><li>For example lets say Jacob is scaling the fence using might 3 and athletics 4 for a dice pool of 7.</li> <li>He has an Enhancement of +2 successes (track shoes and an edge that grants a +1).</li> <li>The Storyguide sets the difficulty as 3 (call it 2 base and 1 complication for a recent rain)</li> </ul><br /> <u><b>Optional</b></u><ul><li>Place Jacobs name here which helps when a lot of peeps are rolling</li> <li>Place a note here maybe scaling the wall so it is easy for the Storyguide to know what you are rolling for</li> </ul><br /> <u><b>No Changes Needed</b></u><ul><li>Target number defaults to 8 and Jacob is not a higher tier so we don't need this.</li> <li>Crit Target (rerolls) defaults to 10 and unless Jacob has a skill trick that effects rerolls we do not need to change this.</li> <li>Double Crits is not needed for the Storypath system</li> </ul><br /> <u><b>Attached Roll</b></u><br /> <br /> In the attached example Jacob nailed the roll with 6 successes. He paid for the 2 difficulty and 1 complication (3 difficulty) leaving 3 successes left over. As the Storyguide I would use these to increase the margin of success of how he scaled the wall, maybe focusing on he was able to do this quickly not costing extra time, stealthy not drawing extra attention, and not leaving any clues behind.<br />